      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your thoughts echo the sentiments of philosophers like Friedrich Nietzsche and Jean-Paul Sartre, who argued that traditional notions of morality and societal expectations can indeed limit individual autonomy. The idea that we're trapped in this 'script' because of fear or external pressures raises questions about the nature of free will and the human condition. If left unchecked, the pursuit of autonomy can lead to a Hobbesian state of \"nasty, brutish, and short\" existence, where individuals prioritize self-preservation above all else.",
